{
  "id": "Compound::DB00431 - Gene::2742",
  "verbalization": "Lindane, a synthetic compound, is shown to bind to Glra3, a subunit of the glycine-gated chloride ion channel, which is involved in the regulation of chloride ion flow across the neuronal membrane. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, with Glra3 participating in various forms of glycine-gated ion channel activity, including extracellular-glycine-gated and extracellular-glycine-gated chloride channel activities. These activities are all linked to the function of Glra2, suggesting a potential role in the modulation of chloride ion channels through the interaction with Glra3. The integrated evidence indicates that Lindane may influence the function of Glra2 by modulating the activity of Glra3, which in turn affects the chloride ion channel activity associated with Glra2. The mechanism is supported by the observed binding and functional participation of Glra3 in the context of Glra2, providing a plausible pathway for the interaction between Lindane and Glra2.",
